# Modbus/TCP write allowlist for the OpenPLC runtime.
#
# Copy to mbwrite_allow.list (next to core/openplc, i.e. the webserver/
# directory the runtime is started from) and restart Modbus. While this file
# is present only the sources listed below may issue Modbus write function
# codes (FC 5, 6, 15, 16) and the debugger function codes (FC 0x41-0x45);
# every other source gets exception 0x01 ILLEGAL FUNCTION. Read function codes
# (FC 1-4) are served to everyone. Without the file all sources may write and
# a warning is logged when the Modbus server starts.
#
# One IPv4 address or CIDR block per line, '#' starts a comment.
# Talon Kingsport Line 4 (see talon/SECURITY-SWARM.md section 3):
172.20.4.10          # Ignition gateway (setpoint writes HR1024-1029)
127.0.0.1            # local OpenPLC Editor / HIL harness
